Core/OSAL/BL616 and BL618DG controllers are supplied by the pinned Bouffalo SDK.
Local changes: enable alternate-setting state outside the lwIP integration;
notify the FreeRTOS+TCP bridge on activation/reset/disconnect.
CDC data interfaces advertise protocol 1 (NCM NTB), required by UsbNcm.sys.
Unused lwIP-only sequence fields are conditional; ncm_tcp.h supplies byte-order
helpers absent in the SDK's older usb_util.h.
Send media/speed notifications on alternate 1 activation (Windows does not
require a packet-filter request), and protect the in-flight notification buffer.
Send SPEED_CHANGE before NETWORK_CONNECTION(up): Windows UsbNcm's adapter
caches link rates and publishes them to NetAdapterCx when link-up is notified.
